cff-version: 1.2.0
title: The Ambiguity Museum
abstract: >-
  A curated collection of cases in which a dispute turned on what a written legal
  instrument actually said, where the words admitted more than one reading and a
  court had to pick one. Each exhibit records the disputed text verbatim with a
  pinpoint, both readings, the holding in the court's own words, what was at stake,
  and the smallest edit that would have forced each reading. Inclusion is governed
  by a machine-checkable schema that admits ambiguity and excludes vagueness.
type: dataset
message: >-
  If you cite an exhibit, cite the underlying judgment. Cite this collection only
  for the curation, the schema, or the aggregate findings.
authors:
  - name: Vichaara Inc.
    city: Portland
    region: Oregon
    country: US
    website: https://vichaara.ai
repository-code: https://github.com/Vichaara/ambiguity-museum
url: https://github.com/Vichaara/ambiguity-museum
license:
